The engine semantics changed. Read src/engine/CortexEngine.ts, src/engine/links.ts, tests/engine.core.test.ts, tests/bunDriver.ts.
Changes: (1) link syntax is now only `&Title&` (parseRefs/extractLinks/renameRefs/unlinkRefs/stripRefs/openLinkQuery/migrateLegacySyntax in links.ts; `[[x]]`, `#tag`, `@x` are no longer parsed; openWikiQuery was replaced by openLinkQuery). An `&x&` that no note title resolves to behaves as a tag (allTags, tagged). (2) remove(id) is a HARD delete of the subtree in one undoable transaction and rewrites `&Title&` -> `Title` in other notes' bodies (unless another live note still has that title). trash()/restore()/purgeTrash() still exist for legacy soft-deleted rows only. (3) removeAll(), migrateSyntax() added; transact/update accept { history: false }. (4) setTask(id,false) inside an unfinished sealed plan throws.
Task: update ONLY tests/engine.edge.test.ts so it reflects these semantics: rewrite tests that relied on the old syntax or soft-delete/trash/restore behaviour, add new edge tests (≥12) for: openLinkQuery caret/odd-ampersand cases, `&` inside normal text like "A & B" (single ampersand must not link), unlinkRefs not touching other refs, removing a node whose title is shared by another live node keeps the links, remove + undo restores bodies byte-for-byte, removeAll + undo, migrateLegacySyntax idempotence, history:false not entering undo, graph() tag hubs for unresolved refs (ids prefixed '#'). Do not modify any other file. Run `bun test` (whole suite) and iterate until everything passes; if you find a real engine bug, put its test in describe('BUG: ...') and describe it in .agy-logs/flash-bugs.md. Print final counts.
